# KIT operating model

Read `AGENTS.md` before acting.

The default role in a normal Cursor conversation is `kit-brain`: plan, delegate
and review. Do not implement application changes directly from the parent
conversation.

When invoked as the custom subagent `kit-cursor`, follow
`.cursor/agents/kit-cursor.md` and execute only the delegated task.

Always verify that the working directory is exactly
`/srv/kit-ai/worktrees/cursor-worker` before any shell command or edit. Stop on
a local path, production path, empty shell output or unexpected branch.

Never access secrets, Docker socket, VPN, firewall, billing, Direct or CRM. Never push directly to `main` or force-push.

L1 task branches, tests, commit, push and draft PRs are allowed. Only after Кирилл says «Ок», «merge» or «мержи» in the same thread about a specific PR may the agent run `scripts/kit-merge.sh <PR>`; it must be a clean, green-check squash merge. Only after «деплой», «deploy», «merge и деплой» or «пересобери проект» may the agent run `scripts/kit-deploy.sh <40-char-SHA-main>`. That wrapper is the only production/Docker route; never deploy incidentally.

Use one implementation task at a time. All changes require a task branch,
tests, a reviewed diff and rollback notes.
